// ============================================================================
// bispectrum.kn — TurboKain 25: 3D Bispectrum & Normalized Bicoherence (b^2)
// Quadratic Phase Coupling (QPC), Non-Linear Harmonic & Intermodulation Engine
//
// Theoretical Foundation:
//   Standard second-order spectral methods (FFT power spectrum, drift_hunt,
//   autocorrelation) discard all phase relationships, remaining fundamentally
//   blind to non-linear wave-wave interactions and phase-locked structures.
//   Furthermore, Gaussian processes (receiver thermal noise, celestial continuum)
//   have an identically zero theoretical bispectrum.
//
//   bispectrum operates directly on baseband voltage buffers by evaluating the
//   third-order cumulant spectrum across segment blocks:
//     1. Direct Bispectrum:
//        B(f1, f2) = E[ X(f1) * X(f2) * X*(f1 + f2) ]
//     2. Normalized Bicoherence (Kim & Powers 1979):
//        b^2(f1, f2) = |B(f1, f2)|^2 / ( E[|X(f1)*X(f2)|^2] * E[|X(f1+f2)|^2] )
//        Bounded strictly in [0.0, 1.0]. Uncoupled Gaussian noise yields b^2 ~ 1/M;
//        exact quadratic phase coupling (QPC) yields b^2 -> 1.0.
//     3. Irreducible Principal Domain (IRPD):
//        Restricts search space strictly to the non-redundant triangle:
//        Omega = { (f1, f2) | 0 <= f2 <= f1, f1 + f2 <= fs / 2 }
//        slashing computational evaluation space by 83.3%.
//     4. Specialized 1D Diagonal Sweep:
//        Evaluates self-harmonic frequency-doubling locks (f2 = f1) in O(N) time.
//
// Semantics & Decision Ladder:
//   * L3 converge: bicoherence_accum verified against reference spec with scalar lane.
//   * L2 law: irpd_domain_ok, bicoherence_bounds, noise_threshold_ok.
//   * L1 world/patch: BispectrumAuthority <-> BispectrumMirror tracking QPC audits.
//   * Memory: Zero-allocation hot loops, +32 byte SIMD padding, single decay.
//
// Exit codes: 0 searched, 1 help / prove FAIL, 2 error.
// ============================================================================

